# Campaign OUTPUT is deliberately not tracked here.
#
# This repository is the library; the analysis inputs to a manuscript belong
# with the manuscript, under the same reproducibility guard as every other
# number in it.  The merged form of these shards is committed in
# catalog-comparison-paper as project/results/precessing_campaign.csv (via
# git-lfs), and the raw shards move to project/results/precessing_campaign/
# once the campaign finishes -- see that repo's paper_plan.md, Phase 6.
#
# Tracking them here as well would mean two sources of truth for the same
# numbers, and these files are rewritten after every simulation while a campaign
# is running, so each commit would add tens of megabytes of churn.
results_*.json
retry_results_*.json
bms_partial_results.json
*.log
*.npz
*.png
*.pdf
*.bak
*.tmp
__pycache__/

# Scratch plotting scripts, superseded by the paper repo's production versions
# (catalog-comparison-paper project/scripts/plot_precessing_results.py, wrapped
# by project/bin/make_fig_*.sh).  Keeping a second copy here would let the two
# drift, and only the paper-repo one is covered by the artifact-script check.
make_figs.py
fig_permode_paper.py

# One-off diagnostic plotters from the frame investigation.  They produced the
# Lhat(t) comparison figures that led to the frame-A/frame-B result, but nothing
# in the manuscript is built from them -- that result is reported from the
# campaign, in catalog-comparison-paper sec:frame_appendix.  Left untracked
# rather than cleaned up to satisfy the hooks, since they are throwaway.
precession_frame/
